# Secrets — never commit
# Pattern-based, not filename-based: an enumerated list only covers the paths someone
# thought of. These cover every .env anywhere in the tree, including backups, while
# still allowing the checked-in templates.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/.credentials.json
claude-accounts*
claude-credentials*

# Agent working directories — may record where secrets live
.agentwork/

# Machine-local config — per-seat absolute paths
.mcp.json
.claude/settings.json
**/.claude/settings.local.json
**/.playwright-mcp/

# Node
**/node_modules/

# Python
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.venv/

# Build and render output (regenerable, often large)
apps/claude-remotion/out/
apps/claude-remotion/build/
apps/claude-remotion/exports/
apps/claude-remotion/previews/
apps/claude-remotion/public/*.mp4
apps/video-reviewer/dist/
/out/

# Logs
*.log

# Generated data for the daily edition
apps/claude-remotion/src/templates/ai_top5/data.json

# Generated/derived media. These are rebuilt by the scripts that own them; committing
# them means the repo carries megabytes whose provenance is a script run nobody recorded.
apps/claude-remotion/public/brand-sting/
apps/claude-remotion/public/narrative-arc/
apps/claude-remotion/public/bridge/

# Third-party and generated audio beds — see studio/ASSET_RECORDS.md for why anything
# under public/ that ships needs a provenance record before it is committed.
apps/claude-remotion/public/audio/*.mp3
!apps/claude-remotion/public/audio/bed.mp3

# Studio video library (studio/FILE_PROTOCOL.md) — finished videos are never committed
studio/output/

# Regenerable studio scraper / audit outputs
studio/social/latest.json
studio/audits/incoming/
studio/brand-packs/*/capture/
studio/brand-packs/*/report.md

# Local caches
.cce/
.DS_Store

# Release working documents. These are the owner's briefs and my reports back during the release
# passes — process, not product. RELEASE_STATE.md and RELEASE_COMPOSITION_TRIAGE.md were kept
# untracked from the start for exactly that reason; RELEASE_FIXES.md and RELEASE_FIXES_2.md were
# committed before that convention existed and are untracked here to match.
#
# They never shipped: the payload build excludes /^RELEASE_[^/]*\.md$/ by pattern. But a
# hand-maintained exclude list is a weaker guarantee than the file simply not being in the tree,
# and the tree is about to be frozen for a clean public history.
/RELEASE_*.md
